@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}

<div class="page-header">
    <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
    <h1>About Bizbox</h1>
</div>

<div style="max-width: 700px;">
    <p>Starting a small business usually means sourcing equipment from several vendors with no single reference point for quality or price. Bizbox addresses this with a curated equipment catalog per business type, plus a resale marketplace so equipment doesn't go to waste when an owner upgrades.</p>

    <p>Bizbox currently supports four business types: Coffee Shop, Bakery, Restaurant, and Salon. Each has its own curated catalog, and every catalog also carries resale listings from other users alongside new equipment.</p>

    <h3 style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">How it works</h3>
    <ol class="steps" style="margin-top: var(--space-4);">
        <li><h3>1. Pick your business type</h3><p class="text-muted">Coffee Shop, Bakery, Restaurant, or Salon.</p></li>
        <li><h3>2. Browse &amp; buy</h3><p class="text-muted">New equipment or resale listings, side by side.</p></li>
        <li><h3>3. Resell when you upgrade</h3><p class="text-muted">List your old equipment instead of it going to waste.</p></li>
    </ol>

    <h3 style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">Scope</h3>
    <p>This is an academic e-commerce project built with ASP.NET Core MVC. Domestic payments run through eSewa and Khalti sandbox integrations; manufacturer listings and international payment are simulated for this project's scope.</p>
</div>
